#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157021 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d9a9b6de-b0dd-5b38-a32b-378d2b1d86a2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Difference of Sets Without a Venn Diagram"}] :question/id #uuid "35acfa60-3395-5f11-94f9-627499386932" :question/math-academy-id "e-7159" :question/problem "Given the sets $X = \\{2, 5, 7, 8 \\}$, $Y = \\{1, 3, 5 \\}$, and $Z = \\{2, 4, 6, 8 \\}$, find $X \\setminus Y$, $Y \\setminus Z$, and $Z \\setminus X$." :question/worked-solution "The set $X \\setminus Y$ is the set of all elements belonging to $X$ but *not* $Y$. Note that the element $5 \\in Y$ is also in $X$, so we must remove it. Hence, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nX∖Y &= X - Y \\\\\n&= {2, 5, 7, 8} - {1, 3, 5} \\\\\n&= {2, 7, 8}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe set $Y \\setminus Z$ is the set of all elements belonging to $Y$ but *not* $Z$. Note that none of the elements of $Y$ are in $Z$. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nY∖Z &= Y - Z \\\\\n&= {1, 3, 5} - {2, 4, 6, 8} \\\\\n&= {1, 3, 5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe set $Z \\setminus X$ is the set of all elements belonging to $Z$ but *not* $X$. Note that the elements $2,8 \\in Z$ are also in $X$, so we must remove them. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nZ∖X &= Z - X \\\\\n&= {2, 4, 6, 8} - {2, 5, 7, 8} \\\\\n&= {4, 6}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157022 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "67e90c94-5018-582f-8692-a1155f41f7c7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Differences of Sets Given Verbally"}] :question/id #uuid "89c94a89-21de-5a4f-a365-85701b2e4ef2" :question/math-academy-id "e-7160" :question/problem "Let $A$ be the set of all multiples of $4$ that are greater than $0$ and let $B$ be the set of all multiples of $6$ that are greater than $0$. What is $A \\setminus B$?" :question/worked-solution "The multiples of $4$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nA = \\{4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32, 36 \\ldots \\}\n$$\n\nLikewise, multiples of $6$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nB = \\{6,12,18,24,30,36,\\ldots \\}\n$$\n\nNow, $A \\setminus B$ is the *difference* of $A$ and $B$, which means that we want to find the elements that are in $A$ but *not* in $B$.\n\nThe elements of $A$ that are also in $B$ are $12, 24, 36$ and so on (i.e. multiples of $12$). So, we must remove these elements from $A$. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA∖B &= A - B \\\\\n&= {4, 8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 28, 32, 36, …} - {6, 12, 18, 24, 30, 36, …} \\\\\n&= {4, 8, 16, 20, 28, 32, …}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157026 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4687dcd7-a5ab-5dc6-be6d-89d806a61a02" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Difference of Sets Using a Venn Diagram"}] :question/id #uuid "9e0d2770-a884-558f-becb-a38fe709b2a5" :question/math-academy-id "e-7167" :question/problem "Given the sets $X = \\{1, 2, 3, 5, 8 \\}$ and $Y = \\{1, 2, 4, 8 \\}$ shown above, find $Y \\setminus X$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2828/Source/Images/a611beb9aa153fcc180f4022a8ae9653.png)" :question/worked-solution "The difference $Y \\setminus X$ consists of all the elements that are in $Y$ but not $X$. To represent $Y \\setminus X$, we will shade in all the area that is contained in $Y$ but not $X$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2828/Source/Images/9b8beaf86d4e877f60560dd050e8ed91.png)\n\nThe only element in $Y$ that is not in $X$ is $4$.\n\nTherefore, the difference is\n\n$$\nY \\setminus X = \\{4 \\}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157703 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d9a9b6de-b0dd-5b38-a32b-378d2b1d86a2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Difference of Sets Without a Venn Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0057fa21-eea2-55af-8ba3-bce91fb99f70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{3, 4, 5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155471} {:answer/id #uuid "0bb45c59-3ae5-5cb4-944c-cef85207ff0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155472} {:answer/id #uuid "39e53930-6c82-5028-80df-d59610b77cd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{6, 9, 10, 15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155473} {:answer/id #uuid "4dc20f73-c893-5a56-a848-99f6a0c8c1f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{3, 4, 5, 5, 7, 9, 10, 15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155474} {:answer/id #uuid "7de6b40e-0ca2-59d0-be8b-9cac8d8e46c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155475}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39e53930-6c82-5028-80df-d59610b77cd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{6, 9, 10, 15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155473} :answer-field/id #uuid "f11d6148-1fa4-5a13-96a4-1334ab6a0152" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155470}] :question/id #uuid "786ea6f6-869f-5532-aea7-ac2eea6a1803" :question/math-academy-id "q-36189" :question/problem "If $A = {3, 4, 5, 6, 9, 10, 15}$ and $B = {3, 4, 5, 7}$, then $A∖B =$"}]}
